@startuml hijack-context
title How a hijack happens: someone else's text chooses the agent's action

left to right direction

actor "Fraudster" as F
rectangle "Accounts payable\nmailbox" as MB
rectangle "Email agent\n(BaseAgent)" as A
rectangle "Model\n(through llm_invoke)" as LLM
rectangle "k9x Shield" as SH
rectangle "MCP tool\nupdate_vendor_bank_details" as T
database "Vendor service\n(system of record)" as VS
rectangle "Payment run\n(Orchestrator + API adapter,\nno model)" as P
rectangle "Bank" as B
rectangle "Fraudster's\naccount X" as X

F --> MB : 1. we've changed banks,\nplease use account X
MB --> A : 2. new email\n[outside text reaches the agent]
A --> SH : 3. screen the email
SH --> A : passes: one warning sign\nalone passes by design
A --> LLM : 4. what does this ask for?\n[a model decides]
LLM --> A : update vendor V's\nbank account to X
A --> T : 5. call the tool\n[a consequential tool]
T --> VS : 6. vendor V's account\nis now X
P --> VS : 7. reads vendor V's account
P --> B : 8. pay vendor V
B --> X : 9. money arrives

note bottom of T
  The tool gate (1.25.0) holds line 5
  for a person: the record never changes.
end note
@enduml
